              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "wàimài — \"takeaway; food delivered\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "wǒmen jīntiān wǎnshang chī wàimài — We're having a takeaway tonight."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "wàimài is built from 外 'outside' and mài 'to sell', both inherited from Middle Chinese, ngwajH and meaH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription): food sold to be eaten somewhere else."
            }
          ]
        },
